00:53:07.519 --> 00:53:09.811
Jab, focus break.


00:53:09.813 --> 00:53:11.857
This is a five board,
step across side kick.


00:53:20.824 --> 00:53:22.407
I hadn't seen Rick
in some time.


00:53:22.409 --> 00:53:25.494
He came to me and said he
wanted to get a black belt.


00:53:25.496 --> 00:53:27.412
We had a discussion
about that because


00:53:27.414 --> 00:53:29.791
at that time, his vision
had gotten worse


00:53:29.793 --> 00:53:31.876
and at the time,
we probably had


00:53:31.878 --> 00:53:34.295
the hardest black belt
test in the country.


00:53:34.297 --> 00:53:35.755
You would go
10 3-minute rounds


00:53:35.757 --> 00:53:38.590
against fresh opponents
with 1 minute's rest.


00:53:38.592 --> 00:53:40.133
Master Douglas
wanted to give me


00:53:40.135 --> 00:53:41.594
an honorary black belt
because he said


00:53:41.596 --> 00:53:42.804
"You've put in your times
and lumps."


00:53:42.806 --> 00:53:44.514
I said,
"No, I wanna earn it


00:53:44.516 --> 00:53:46.724
the same way you and Terry
and everybody else did.


00:53:46.726 --> 00:53:49.309
I wanna go the 10
3-minute rounds."


00:53:49.311 --> 00:53:50.561
He wanted it
to mean something


00:53:50.563 --> 00:53:53.023
so we started training.


00:53:57.695 --> 00:53:59.737
The test
is very difficult


00:53:59.739 --> 00:54:01.780
for anyone
under any circumstance.


00:54:01.782 --> 00:54:04.075
You can be an incredibly
gifted athlete.


00:54:04.077 --> 00:54:05.867
You're gonna be tested.


00:54:05.869 --> 00:54:08.746
When you fight
10 fresh fighters


00:54:08.748 --> 00:54:11.039
and they're all tough and
they're all out to get you


00:54:11.041 --> 00:54:14.584
you're gonna pay
a hefty price.


00:54:14.586 --> 00:54:16.586
Now the final point.
You're legally blind.


00:54:16.588 --> 00:54:18.296
Yeah, and I don't see
very well either.


00:54:18.298 --> 00:54:20.758
Well, how could you
possibly fight?


00:54:20.760 --> 00:54:21.925
I don't know?
We'll find out.


00:54:21.927 --> 00:54:23.221
Sit and watch.


00:54:24.931 --> 00:54:27.474
- Chin in. Chin in.
- Come on, Rick.


00:54:32.480 --> 00:54:34.731
It was full contact.


00:54:34.733 --> 00:54:36.106
This was not a man


00:54:36.108 --> 00:54:37.693
who was visually impaired
to them.


00:54:41.822 --> 00:54:42.781
Come on, Rick.


00:54:44.117 --> 00:54:45.657
I caught a roundhouse kick
right here


00:54:45.659 --> 00:54:47.452
and snapped this bone
right here, so I fought


00:54:47.454 --> 00:54:48.661
the last
3 and a half rounds


00:54:48.663 --> 00:54:50.371
with a broken
right arm.


00:54:51.791 --> 00:54:53.624
- Keep going.
- You got it.


00:54:59.132 --> 00:55:01.298
It was probably
the only time


00:55:01.300 --> 00:55:04.885
I have seen Rick
almost broken.


00:55:04.887 --> 00:55:07.304
It was probably
a little bit too brutal


00:55:07.306 --> 00:55:09.224
but we didn't want it
to be a gift.


00:55:19.652 --> 00:55:21.693
Getting my black belt
was one of my single


00:55:21.695 --> 00:55:23.114
greatest
accomplishments.


00:55:24.824 --> 00:55:26.449
It took me 13 years


00:55:26.451 --> 00:55:28.909
3 months and 6 days


00:55:28.911 --> 00:55:31.537
and the next day, the whole
bloody mess was spread across


00:55:31.539 --> 00:55:35.666
the front page of "Los Angeles
Times" sports section.


00:55:35.668 --> 00:55:38.168
The only thing is,
they used the word blind


00:55:38.170 --> 00:55:40.338
so I never showed
anybody that article


00:55:40.340 --> 00:55:42.255
because they had
to put the Blind Man


00:55:42.257 --> 00:55:44.717
Earns Black Belt
in there.


00:55:44.719 --> 00:55:47.429
I want my stuff
to stand on its own.


00:55:52.601 --> 00:55:54.811
You got one
from Jim Blowers.


00:55:54.813 --> 00:55:56.896
- Mom read that to me.
- Doug.


00:55:56.898 --> 00:55:58.231
Doug Gorman.
Mom read that to me.


00:55:58.233 --> 00:56:01.525
Okay. You got one
from the AMAs.


00:56:01.527 --> 00:56:03.778
The Academy
of Magical Arts.


00:56:03.780 --> 00:56:04.945
Oh, read it.
What does it say?


00:56:04.947 --> 00:56:06.697
Uh..


00:56:06.699 --> 00:56:10.367
It says,
"Richard, congratulations.


00:56:10.369 --> 00:56:11.702
"Once again,
you have been nominated


00:56:11.704 --> 00:56:13.454
"as the Close-Up Magician
of the Year


00:56:13.456 --> 00:56:16.289
by the members of The
Academy of Magical Arts."


00:56:16.291 --> 00:56:18.208
I've been nominated
for a 2nd year in a row.


00:56:18.210 --> 00:56:20.211
2nd year in a row.
I have to say, okay.


00:56:20.213 --> 00:56:23.800
And, uh, you have to respond
with your acceptance.


00:56:26.385 --> 00:56:27.885
As his publicist,
I can tell you


00:56:27.887 --> 00:56:29.387
I've already
written his speech.


00:56:29.389 --> 00:56:31.639
Uh, thank you
very much.


00:56:31.641 --> 00:56:33.182
No.


00:56:33.184 --> 00:56:34.726
You have to say
more than that.


00:56:34.728 --> 00:56:36.144
Uh..


00:56:36.146 --> 00:56:37.644
Whatever happens
at that moment


00:56:37.646 --> 00:56:39.396
is what's gonna happen
at that moment.


00:56:39.398 --> 00:56:44.151
No, you should not do
an extemporaneous speech.


00:56:44.153 --> 00:56:45.737
You'll regret
everything you said


00:56:45.739 --> 00:56:47.655
and you'll regret
everything you didn't say.


00:56:47.657 --> 00:56:49.157
Well, okay, it's going
to be short and sweet.


00:56:49.159 --> 00:56:51.992
"Hello. Thank you.
Thank you.


00:56:51.994 --> 00:56:54.454
And thank you. Goodbye."


00:56:54.456 --> 00:56:55.454
Is that good?


00:56:55.456 --> 00:56:56.706
I'll be writing him
a speech.


00:57:05.050 --> 00:57:07.592
I've been nominated as
Close-Up Magician of the Year


00:57:07.594 --> 00:57:10.219
by The Academy
of Magical Arts.


00:57:10.221 --> 00:57:13.930
In our business, this is the
equivalent of the Oscars.


00:57:13.932 --> 00:57:16.934
There hasn't been
a single card mechanic


00:57:16.936 --> 00:57:19.519
that has actually
won this award.


00:57:19.521 --> 00:57:22.523
So to finally be
acknowledged and honored


00:57:22.525 --> 00:57:24.775
for what I have spent
a lifetime developing


00:57:24.777 --> 00:57:26.904
would be quite
an achievement.


00:57:29.532 --> 00:57:31.407
The first time we came,
we were very hopeful.


00:57:31.409 --> 00:57:33.950
You know, your first
nomination is the big deal.


00:57:33.952 --> 00:57:36.454
We had hopes and clearly,
Rick was disappointed


00:57:36.456 --> 00:57:38.831
as was I
when he didn't make it.


00:57:38.833 --> 00:57:40.041
I kind of have
that feeling


00:57:40.043 --> 00:57:42.293
this year
that he's gonna win.


00:57:42.295 --> 00:57:44.798
I hope I'm right
for his sake.


00:57:48.927 --> 00:57:51.554
Asa, your dad wants you
to see what he has on.


00:57:53.972 --> 00:57:55.932
What do you say?


00:57:55.934 --> 00:57:57.766
Your tie's not
tied right.


00:57:57.768 --> 00:58:00.311
The tie doesn't?
Too long, too short?


00:58:00.313 --> 00:58:01.646
Knot's wrong.


00:58:01.648 --> 00:58:02.979
Knot's wrong
for this dress?


00:58:02.981 --> 00:58:04.315
Uh-huh.
The purse matches.


00:58:07.070 --> 00:58:09.698
Okay, time to, I'll try
the other one on instead.


00:58:13.867 --> 00:58:18.662
To think that the same
scared visually-impaired kid


00:58:18.664 --> 00:58:21.666
sitting around shuffling
cards in the VH room


00:58:21.668 --> 00:58:23.501
could be
on stage tonight


00:58:23.503 --> 00:58:26.838
receiving this award
is humbling.


00:58:26.840 --> 00:58:29.840
59 years old,
finally wearin' a tie.


00:58:29.842 --> 00:58:31.008
I'm so proud.


00:58:31.010 --> 00:58:32.342
And then you're just
gonna wanna


00:58:32.344 --> 00:58:33.970
just tighten it up
just a tad bit.


00:58:33.972 --> 00:58:35.679
That's why I never
learned how to tie a tie.


00:58:35.681 --> 00:58:37.347
I wore those
Colonel Sanders ties


00:58:37.349 --> 00:58:38.893
for 30 somethin' years.


00:58:40.686 --> 00:58:43.647
Uh-huh. I think
I'm too long this time.


00:58:45.400 --> 00:58:47.150
Alright, lift up your chin
so I can get your neck.


00:58:47.152 --> 00:58:49.193
Did you already shave
this morning?


00:58:49.195 --> 00:58:52.530
Alright, let me put a little
bit of water on your hair.


00:58:52.532 --> 00:58:55.575
There you go.
And on your mustache.


00:58:55.577 --> 00:58:57.784
I think that
in his heart's desire


00:58:57.786 --> 00:59:00.371
he would like to step up
his recognition


00:59:00.373 --> 00:59:02.206
in the performing world.


00:59:02.208 --> 00:59:04.374
And my biggest fear
for him is that


00:59:04.376 --> 00:59:06.001
he would not
achieve that.


00:59:06.003 --> 00:59:07.211
Winner.


00:59:21.686 --> 00:59:24.103
Ladies and gentlemen


00:59:24.105 --> 00:59:28.068
welcome to the 46th
Annual AMA Awards.


00:59:38.911 --> 00:59:41.829
Hey, hey! Help me down!
Oh, yes!


00:59:41.831 --> 00:59:43.458
Oh, yes! Thank you!


00:59:45.418 --> 00:59:47.126
- Thank you very much!
- Thank you, everybody!


00:59:47.128 --> 00:59:48.670
- Have a good night!
- You guys are great!


00:59:48.672 --> 00:59:50.630
Have a good night!


00:59:50.632 --> 00:59:53.965
And now it's time
for the Close-Up Magician


00:59:53.967 --> 00:59:55.510
of the Year award.


00:59:55.512 --> 00:59:58.137
The nominees
for the 2013


00:59:58.139 --> 01:00:00.599
Close-Up Magician
of the Year are..


01:00:01.934 --> 01:00:03.726
Bill Goodwin.


01:00:06.981 --> 01:00:08.981
Helder Guimaraes.


01:00:10.777 --> 01:00:12.818
Armando Lucero.


01:00:14.989 --> 01:00:16.949
David Regal.


01:00:18.159 --> 01:00:20.450
Richard Turner.


01:00:23.123 --> 01:00:25.625
And the winner is..


01:00:27.501 --> 01:00:28.793
...Bill Goodwin!


01:01:16.175 --> 01:01:18.508
Today, our son


01:01:18.510 --> 01:01:21.389
is off to university.


01:01:22.599 --> 01:01:26.311
I... I'm so proud
of him, obviously.


01:01:31.900 --> 01:01:35.025
He's been my partner
for 18 years.


01:01:35.027 --> 01:01:36.193
I mean, he started
traveling with me


01:01:36.195 --> 01:01:38.987
when he was a baby.


01:01:38.989 --> 01:01:42.282
For the first ten years
of his life


01:01:42.284 --> 01:01:45.288
I... I, I could
feel him growing.


01:01:46.664 --> 01:01:48.456
Now, he's stronger
than the old man


01:01:48.458 --> 01:01:50.541
smarter than
the old man


01:01:50.543 --> 01:01:53.963
handsomer than the
old man, and, uh..


01:01:56.840 --> 01:01:58.842
My wife and I
are so proud of him.


01:02:06.768 --> 01:02:08.728
Is that you
opening the door?


01:02:11.231 --> 01:02:13.146
- Asa?
- Yeah.


01:02:13.148 --> 01:02:14.981
I just don't want
to walk off any cliff.


01:02:14.983 --> 01:02:16.191
There's no cliff, dad..


01:02:16.193 --> 01:02:17.401
People say,
"Is he going to follow


01:02:17.403 --> 01:02:18.695
in his father's
footsteps?"


01:02:18.697 --> 01:02:21.905
I say, "He's too smart
to try to do that."


01:02:21.907 --> 01:02:23.740
You know, he's going to,
he's going to take things


01:02:23.742 --> 01:02:26.371
to levels
beyond what I did.


01:02:27.914 --> 01:02:31.249
I played with cards and
I've done well with it


01:02:31.251 --> 01:02:33.501
and it's been fun
and it's exciting


01:02:33.503 --> 01:02:35.628
but he's gonna do
more substantial things.


01:02:35.630 --> 01:02:38.298
Make a greater impact
on society.


01:02:39.634 --> 01:02:41.092
Alright.
Behave yourself.


01:02:41.094 --> 01:02:42.262
I will.


01:02:43.471 --> 01:02:44.929
Adios, amigo.


01:02:44.931 --> 01:02:47.974
- Spiderman, love you, man.
- You too.


01:02:47.976 --> 01:02:49.686
- You have fun, okay?
- I will.


01:03:12.541 --> 01:03:15.961
Get that card.
Get that renegade.


01:03:23.719 --> 01:03:26.180
Well, another one
bites the dust.


01:03:36.648 --> 01:03:38.483
Hey, Johnny.


01:03:38.485 --> 01:03:42.235
I was taking a minute off
of the spinning wheel


01:03:42.237 --> 01:03:45.113
and walking the dog.


01:03:45.115 --> 01:03:48.325
A few one-hand middles
and, uh


01:03:48.327 --> 01:03:50.661
thought I'd give you
a harassment call.


01:03:50.663 --> 01:03:52.623
Well, talk to you.
Later.


01:03:55.168 --> 01:03:57.418
You know, when Asa
first flew the coup


01:03:57.420 --> 01:03:59.420
it was really hard, and it
was really hard on Rick


01:03:59.422 --> 01:04:01.171
because he really likes
having Asa here


01:04:01.173 --> 01:04:03.634
to run him places
and do things.


01:04:05.177 --> 01:04:06.344
I have heard
Rick complain


01:04:06.346 --> 01:04:08.887
about his vision.


01:04:08.889 --> 01:04:11.016
And he gets
really frustrated.


01:04:13.353 --> 01:04:15.603
When he's down
in spirit


01:04:15.605 --> 01:04:19.356
he doesn't really like to
show that to other people.


01:04:19.358 --> 01:04:22.693
He always wants to be
seen as the strong person


01:04:22.695 --> 01:04:24.987
and he doesn't
ever want anyone


01:04:24.989 --> 01:04:26.990
to think
that he's weak.


01:04:36.208 --> 01:04:37.708
I was told
way back when


01:04:37.710 --> 01:04:39.753
you will eventually
lose all your sight.


01:04:41.380 --> 01:04:43.923
When I got married,
I never told Kim


01:04:43.925 --> 01:04:46.720
and I probably should
have, but I never did.


01:04:48.346 --> 01:04:50.262
I guess you could say
I was afraid


01:04:50.264 --> 01:04:52.472
but I thought
I have what I have


01:04:52.474 --> 01:04:56.144
and I'm not gonna... I'm not
gonna accept anything less


01:04:56.146 --> 01:04:58.523
even though
the less kept coming.


01:05:01.358 --> 01:05:02.608
In our lifetime
together


01:05:02.610 --> 01:05:04.570
it's happened
like three times.


01:05:05.362 --> 01:05:06.570
When we got married


01:05:06.572 --> 01:05:08.072
he could still see
pretty good.


01:05:08.074 --> 01:05:11.784
I mean, he walked around
without any help.


01:05:11.786 --> 01:05:14.327
And then, all of a sudden,
he took a dip


01:05:14.329 --> 01:05:17.414
and I think
he knew it happened


01:05:17.416 --> 01:05:20.001
but he didn't want to
admit that it happened


01:05:20.003 --> 01:05:22.920
and so finally one day,
he came to me...


01:05:22.922 --> 01:05:24.755
You all are going
to make me cry.


01:05:24.757 --> 01:05:25.882
He said, "Do you know,
I don't think


01:05:25.884 --> 01:05:27.842
I can see
very well anymore."


01:05:27.844 --> 01:05:31.095
And so that was
really, really hard.


01:05:31.097 --> 01:05:33.722
And then, I'm gonna say
about ten years later


01:05:33.724 --> 01:05:35.184
there was nothing.


01:05:36.686 --> 01:05:39.269
I have to say it probably
took me a year


01:05:39.271 --> 01:05:41.856
before I realized that
what I was seeing


01:05:41.858 --> 01:05:44.566
was not what was there.


01:05:44.568 --> 01:05:46.235
The thing is
if I do this


01:05:46.237 --> 01:05:48.070
I will see


01:05:48.072 --> 01:05:49.572
uh, just like a clock
going back and forth


01:05:49.574 --> 01:05:50.782
my hand go back
and forth


01:05:50.784 --> 01:05:51.949
but if I close my eyes


01:05:51.951 --> 01:05:53.784
I see the exact
same thing.


01:05:53.786 --> 01:05:56.454
And I realized
it's not real.


01:05:56.456 --> 01:05:59.874
I... I'm not seeing anything
that's real anymore.


01:05:59.876 --> 01:06:03.086
I didn't realize
all that was left was


01:06:03.088 --> 01:06:04.878
how my mind filled
in the blanks


01:06:04.880 --> 01:06:07.800
rather than through any
kind of visual sight.


01:06:12.054 --> 01:06:14.889
When I lost
the rest of my vision


01:06:14.891 --> 01:06:17.057
I lost the independence
that I had.


01:06:17.059 --> 01:06:20.061
Before, I could walk
alongside somebody


01:06:20.063 --> 01:06:22.854
and not have to be touching
them or them touching me


01:06:22.856 --> 01:06:24.648
and when I lost that


01:06:24.650 --> 01:06:26.818
that meant
as much to me as


01:06:26.820 --> 01:06:29.072
for anyone else to have
lost their vision.


01:06:30.824 --> 01:06:34.242
That was really hard
for all of us


01:06:34.244 --> 01:06:36.661
because, first of all,
Rick wouldn't admit it.


01:06:36.663 --> 01:06:38.579
Even though
we all knew it.


01:06:38.581 --> 01:06:40.748
And he wasn't gonna
change his lifestyle


01:06:40.750 --> 01:06:41.999
you know,
he was Rick, man.


01:06:42.001 --> 01:06:44.001
He can overcome
anything.


01:06:44.003 --> 01:06:47.005
I did not want
to be helped.


01:06:47.007 --> 01:06:48.338
It was
very humbling to go


01:06:48.340 --> 01:06:51.383
from a self-sufficient
disabled person


01:06:51.385 --> 01:06:54.346
to a dependent
disabled person.


01:06:56.224 --> 01:06:59.851
He really was relying
very heavily on myself


01:06:59.853 --> 01:07:03.311
to help him with
everything that he needed.


01:07:03.313 --> 01:07:05.731
I remember having
to actually say


01:07:05.733 --> 01:07:08.358
that I felt like he was
using me, kind of...


01:07:08.360 --> 01:07:11.028
I felt like I was his,
like a Seeing Eye dog.


01:07:11.030 --> 01:07:12.572
Which was terrible
because when he needed me


01:07:12.574 --> 01:07:14.365
he'd whistle for me.


01:07:14.367 --> 01:07:16.700
And, at first,
it was okay


01:07:16.702 --> 01:07:17.784
but then I was
starting to think


01:07:17.786 --> 01:07:21.039
"Wow. I just,
I don't like that."


01:07:21.041 --> 01:07:24.208
One day, things had just gone
wrong and life just sucked


01:07:24.210 --> 01:07:26.501
and nothing was happening
the way it should


01:07:26.503 --> 01:07:29.338
and we did the only
thing that we could do


01:07:29.340 --> 01:07:31.048
is that
we hugged each other


01:07:31.050 --> 01:07:32.215
we prayed about it


01:07:32.217 --> 01:07:34.385
and we just agreed that


01:07:34.387 --> 01:07:36.389
we would get
through it together.


01:07:43.271 --> 01:07:47.731
A, B, C, D, E, F


01:07:47.733 --> 01:07:49.733
G, H, I, J


01:07:49.735 --> 01:07:53.570
K, L, M, N...
Zero. Hyphen.


01:07:53.572 --> 01:07:55.072
Oh, be careful touching
some of these things.


01:07:55.074 --> 01:07:56.199
Okay.


01:07:56.201 --> 01:07:57.450
Because you might
turn the voice off.


01:07:57.452 --> 01:07:58.700
Okay. Gotcha. Okay.


01:07:58.702 --> 01:08:01.079
So, the first thing
when you get on your phone


01:08:01.081 --> 01:08:03.581
usually, you wake it up,
right?


01:08:03.583 --> 01:08:05.624
Uh, well, I slap it
a couple of times.


